                <pb facs="0618" n="520" sameAs="frus:frus1900/pg520"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. White to Mr. Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Embassy of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1900-01-23"><hi rendition="#italic">January 23,
                        1900</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1164.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inform you of the
                    receipt to-day from the Imperial foreign office of a note in which reference is
                    made to a request recently addressed by our consul at Kehl to the authorities of
                    Alsace-Lorraine in regard to the whereabouts of one Oskar H. Schneider. It
                    appears that a reward has been offered by our postal authorities for the
                    apprehension of said Schneider and that it was thought possible that he might be
                    found in the house of his brother-in-law, in Alsace. In the note it is stated
                    that nothing has as yet been ascertained in regard to Schneider, and a further
                    communication is promised in case he should be found subsequently. My attention
                    is called to the fact, however, and it is on this account that I report the
                    matter to you, that “extradition between Alsace-Lorraine and the United States
                    is not regulated by treaty” (Auslieferung zwischen Elsass-Lothringen und den
                    Vereinigten Staaten von Amerika nicht vertragsmässig geregelt ist).</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">And. D. White.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
